<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  THE TRAILING ICON BUTTON'S OPTICAL PULL — view_row.xml's @id/row_icon_action.
  ============================================================================

  A file of its own and not an addition to values/dimens.xml, because these two
  numbers belong to the universal row alone: nothing else may reach for them, and
  they are not a spacing step.

  This is ToolbarBinder.alignInkToGutter's problem again, one component down, and
  it takes the same answer: what the eye lines a column up by is the GLYPH's last
  painted pixel, never the edge of the invisible touch target it is centred in.

  view_row.xml's trailing slot holds one of several objects and they are not the
  same KIND of object:

    · @id/row_chevron / @id/row_trailing_glyph are 18dp ImageViews. Their box sits
      on the row's 16dp end padding and the glyph very nearly fills it.
    · @id/row_icon_action is a MaterialButton wearing
      @style/Widget.Departament.Button.Icon: a 22dp icon optically centred in a
      48dp touch minimum, so 13dp of that box is AIR on the trailing side before
      the icon starts.

  Measured off the drawables rather than guessed — every glyph in this set is a
  24-unit viewport, and an ImageView at @dimen/glyph_18 fitCenters it to 18dp
  (× 0.75) while the button draws it at 22dp (× 0.9167). Distance from the row's
  end EDGE to the last painted pixel:

                          box air   glyph air        ink lands at
      ic_chevron_right       0       8 × 0.75  = 6.00     22.00   <- THE DATUM
      ic_arrow_drop_down     0       7 × 0.75  = 5.25     21.25
      ic_action_done         0       3 × 0.75  = 2.25     18.25
      ic_copy               13       3 × 0.917 = 2.75     31.75
      ic_more_vert_24dp     13      10 × 0.917 = 9.17     38.17

  So one card can draw a chevron 22dp from its edge and a copy button 32dp from it,
  and the owner read exactly that: «дальше баги по кнопкам 1-3 скрины, они улетели
  куда-то влево». The chevron is the datum because it is the trailing control the
  product has most of, and because it is the one on «О приложении» that he did NOT
  name — the two offenders share that screen with it.

  ONE NUMBER CANNOT SERVE BOTH GLYPHS, which is the trap the toolbar hit first:
  «⋮» is a 4-unit column of dots in a 24-unit box and «копировать» is a 19-unit
  frame in one, so they are 6.4dp apart before anything is moved. The correction is
  therefore per glyph and lives in RowBinder, at the one place that knows which
  glyph is going in.

  NEITHER PULL COSTS A PIXEL OF TOUCH TARGET. The 48dp box keeps all 48; only where
  it is drawn moves. And both stay INSIDE the row: the row's own paddingEnd is 16,
  so a pull of up to 16 travels through padding the row already owns and nothing is
  clipped.
-->
<resources>

    <!--
        ic_copy: ink 2…21 of 24, i.e. 2.75dp of air at 22dp.
        31.75 − 10 = 21.75, a quarter of a dp inside the chevron's 22.00.
        The 48dp box then ends 6dp short of the card's edge — the same clearance
        @dimen/optical_nudge_touch_target leaves on the leading side of the
        subscription card, which is the shipped precedent for this shape.
    -->
    <dimen name="row_action_nudge_wide">-10dp</dimen>

    <!--
        ic_more_vert_24dp: ink 10…14 of 24, i.e. 9.17dp of air at 22dp.
        38.17 − 16 = 22.17, a sixth of a dp outside the chevron's 22.00.

        SIXTEEN IS THE ROW'S WHOLE END GUTTER, and this control gives all of it
        back: the glyph is so narrow that its own box has to travel the full
        padding for the ink to reach the line. The 48dp target then ends flush with
        the card's edge, which view_toolbar.xml already settled on the other side —
        «the target reaching the screen edge is a Fitts's-law gain rather than a
        cost». The press plate is a disc whose widest point is at the row's vertical
        centre, well clear of the card's 20dp corners, so flush is tangent and never
        a shear.

        This is also the owner's standing request on this glyph, already honoured in
        the toolbar: «три точки которые сверху справа их бы тоже чутка правее
        сделать и это касается везде где они есть».
    -->
    <dimen name="row_action_nudge_overflow">-16dp</dimen>

</resources>
